                        "entry_id": "34258184-e666-3057-9f99-472b394e963b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A piece of armor which protects the arm."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3fc83ef4-6a8c-454d-ae64-1bb3ee60180b",
                                "sense_id": "0354be4d-1d38-3480-b14d-fda246acbd47",
                                "text": "The gardebras here probably implies the whole armour for the arms, consisting of pauldrons, brassarts, elbow-pieces, and vambraces, though there is a gardebras of the more antient kind so formed as to screw on the bridle-arm […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "381c4afb-238c-4228-b847-e662333ad503",
                                "sense_id": "0354be4d-1d38-3480-b14d-fda246acbd47",
                                "text": "The Bishop's silver-gilt \"wardebras,\" the gardebras, or bracer, to protect the left arm, was of singularly costly material."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a7fd12b-08b7-4e13-98f0-709bb8bbdd5f",
                                "sense_id": "0354be4d-1d38-3480-b14d-fda246acbd47",
                                "text": "The gardebras was a separate piece which overlaid and protected the junctures of the armor at the shoulder and elbow."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
